Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: Many medicines interact with prednisone. Some change how much prednisone is in your body, and others add to its side effects. Tell your doctor about every medicine you take, including anything you start or stop during treatment. Be especially careful with:
- medicines that raise prednisone levels, such as ketoconazole, itraconazole, posaconazole, voriconazole, clarithromycin, and some HIV and hepatitis C medicines;
- medicines that lower prednisone levels and can make it work less well, such as rifampin, rifabutin, rifapentine, carbamazepine, phenytoin, phenobarbital, primidone and St. John's wort;
- NSAIDs and aspirin, which raise the risk of stomach ulcers and bleeding;
- blood thinners such as warfarin, since prednisone can change how your blood clots and you may need extra monitoring;
- insulin and diabetes tablets, since prednisone raises blood sugar and your doses may need to go up;
- diuretics (water pills) and amphotericin B, which can lower potassium further;
- digoxin, which is more likely to cause problems if your potassium is low;
Triplet: ["prednisone", "has effect on", "blood sugar"]

The relation 'has effect on' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug influences or alters the physiological process or parameter specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'affects': The subject drug may influence or impact the physiological or developmental process specified by the object entity.
B. 'has effect': The subject drug produces the therapeutic or physiological effect specified by the object entity.
C. 'increases effect of': The subject drug enhances or potentiates the effect of the substance or condition specified by the object entity.
D. 'requires adjustment of': The subject drug necessitates changes or modifications to the treatment or dosage specified by the object entity.
E. 'interacts with': The subject drug has a drug interaction with the drug or substance specified by the object entity that may change effects or cause harm.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
